    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0125" n="113" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg113"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.116/2644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-22">March 22, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador agreed that the British Government should give out the statement
                    accompanying his letter to me of yesterday’s date<anchor n="51" xml:id="d95-f1"
                    /> explaining the British license policy and the less injurious effects that
                    such policy would have on our exports of agricultural products than an absolute
                    embargo with the resulting harmful impression created in this country. I readily
                    agreed with him that this statement to be most effective should be put out at
                    London rather than by the British Embassy in Washington.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="51" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Letter dated March 20, received in the Department March 21, not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
